### Prepared Deployment Steps for IBM Cloud Code Engine:

1. Log in to IBM Cloud:
   $ ibmcloud login -u <IBM_ACCOUNT_EMAIL> --sso

2. Target resource group and region:
   $ ibmcloud target -g Default -r us-south

3. Create or select a Code Engine Project:
   $ ibmcloud ce project create --name dealership-portal
   $ ibmcloud ce project select --name dealership-portal

4. Build and push container images to IBM Cloud Container Registry (ICR):
   $ ibmcloud cr login
   $ docker build -t us.icr.io/<namespace>/dealership-django:latest ./server
   $ docker push us.icr.io/<namespace>/dealership-django:latest

5. Deploy Application on Code Engine:
   $ ibmcloud ce application create --name dealership-django \
       --image us.icr.io/<namespace>/dealership-django:latest \
       --port 8000 \
       --env backend_url=http://dealership-node:3030 \
       --env sentiment_analyzer_url=http://dealership-sentiment:5050/ \
       --min-scale 1 --max-scale 3

6. Retrieve Deployed URL:
   $ ibmcloud ce application get --name dealership-django --output url
   Expected format: https://dealership-django.<random-hash>.<region>.codeengine.appdomain.cloud/

All Dockerfile, entrypoint.sh, and docker-compose configurations are ready in the repository for immediate execution once IBM Cloud credentials are authenticated.
